bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_call_through_non_callable_scalar_segfaults_2026-11-28, 0, "Under the seed strict JIT (SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=jit SIMPLE_JIT_STRICT=1) a call whose callee is a local holding a non-callable scalar segfaults (rc 139) instead of failing to compile. Minimal: fn main(): val n = 5 / print(n(4)). The same happens for a text local: val s = \"x\" / print(s(4)). Reproduced on the seed built from work/jit-pass-keyword-20261128 (sha256 fc6d0a55c15f722a). The sibling fix for seed_jit_call_to_function_named_pass_segfaults_2026-11-28 made a tuple/unit callee a MIR lowering error in the indirect-call branch of lower_call_expr, but deliberately left scalars alone: an i64 local can legitimately hold a function handle in low-level code, so rejecting every integer callee needs a census of src/ first. Fix direction: reject callees whose declared HIR type is text/bool/float outright, and for integer callees either require an explicit function type or prove no in-tree code calls through an i64 handle; never emit IndirectCall through a value known not to be a function."

